---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Container from '../../components/Container.astro';
import SectionIntro from '../../components/SectionIntro.astro';
import TopicCluster from '../../components/TopicCluster.astro';
import FaqList from '../../components/FaqList.astro';
import FaqItem from '../../components/FaqItem.astro';
import SiteCta from '../../components/SiteCta.astro';
import TextLink from '../../components/TextLink.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Remembering | She Who Remembers"
  description="A deeper journey for women in identity transition: rebuilding self-trust, embodiment, and inner coherence without performing a new personality."
>
  <Hero
    heading="The Remembering"
    lede="A Deeper Return to Self"
    surface="light"
    spacing="compact"
  >
    <p>
      This is the flagship journey of She Who Remembers. Not a makeover. A longer return to the
      woman who is no longer willing to live as a well-managed edition of herself.
    </p>
  </Hero>

  <Section surface="dark" atmosphere={true} spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <blockquote class="core-question">
        Who are you when you stop organizing your life around the version of you that everyone
        else already understands?
      </blockquote>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="The threshold">
        <p>
          An old calendar can still fill. People can still be loved. Work can still get done.
          And underneath the competence, the shape of the life no longer feels fully true.
        </p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This does not have to look like crisis. It can look like a quiet mismatch that has
          become harder to talk yourself out of. The life is real. It is also no longer the
          whole of you. The Remembering is for that in-between: not collapsed, not finished,
          unwilling to keep performing a self that has already moved.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="Who this is for">
        <p>Women whose inner weather has changed, with or without a public plot twist.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Some arrive in the middle of an obvious passage: a relationship ending or rearranging,
          burnout that rest did not fix, a career that changed shape, caregiving that rewrote
          the days, motherhood or the years after it, aging that will not stay cosmetic. Some
          arrive through spiritual questions that outgrew the language they were given.
        </p>
        <p>
          Others have no event to point to. Only a growing sense that the woman the world still
          knows how to address is not the one doing the living. That is enough.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="What often brings women here">
        <p>Not a diagnosis. A pattern of self-distance that has become expensive.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <ul class="fit">
        <li>Self-trust thinned by too many second opinions, including your own overthinking.</li>
        <li>Intuition noticed, then overridden, then treated as unreliable because it was ignored.</li>
        <li>Relational roles that still run the room: the fixer, the translator, the one who can.</li>
        <li>Heat in the body with no clean sentence attached to it yet.</li>
        <li>Creativity that went dormant while everything else stayed impressive.</li>
        <li>Over-functioning that looks like devotion from the outside and exile from the inside.</li>
        <li>A body that is asked to carry the life, but is rarely asked before a decision is made.</li>
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container>
      <SectionIntro heading="What the journey holds">
        <p>
          These are fields of practice, not badges. You will not be asked to master all of them
          in order to belong.
        </p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="topics">
        <TopicCluster title="Sovereignty">Identity, choice, and self-command: the return of an inner vote.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Shadow">Anger, jealousy, fear, and the truths that were sent underground to keep you acceptable.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Embodiment">Body, breath, and presence: becoming legible to yourself in real time.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Voice">Expression, boundaries, and speech that does not rush to make itself palatable.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Intuition">Discernment, evidence, timing, and self-trust that can tell anxiety from knowing.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Relationship">Connection that does not require you to disappear in order to stay loved.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Creation">Desire, making, and living expression that is not a performance of healing.</TopicCluster>
        <TopicCluster title="Legacy">What becomes possible when repair is no longer the center of identity.</TopicCluster>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="Five movements">
        <p>
          The Remembering sits inside a larger path. The movements are named here so you can
          feel the weather, not so you can memorize a syllabus.
        </p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <ol class="movements">
        <li>
          <span>Awakening.</span> Catching the places you stopped consulting yourself.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>Descent.</span> Meeting what was hidden to remain acceptable.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>Embodiment.</span> Letting insight arrive in breath, voice, and choice.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>Ascent.</span> Returning life to the center once more of you is available.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>Legacy.</span> Asking what continues because you became conscious.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="work-link">
        The fuller philosophy lives on
        <TextLink href={withBase('/the-work')}>The Work</TextLink>.
        This page is the doorway, not a second map.
      </p>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="What participation feels like">
        <p>Serious work can still leave room for a human nervous system.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Expect reflection, embodied practice, and choices you can actually use on a Tuesday.
          There is no forced disclosure, and no prize for performing vulnerability. Humor is
          allowed. So is privacy. You do not need a spiritual belief system to take part. The
          invitation is integration: bringing what you know into how you speak, rest, create,
          and stay in relationship without abandoning yourself.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="What this work is not">
        <p>The edges matter. They keep the journey from becoming a costume.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <ul class="not">
        <li>It is not therapy, diagnosis, or a treatment plan.</li>
        <li>It is not a school for performing femininity, softness, or desirability.</li>
        <li>It is not training in polarity, seduction, or relationship manipulation.</li>
        <li>It is not a claim of spiritual superiority, and it does not sell guaranteed awakening.</li>
        <li>It does not require you to narrate trauma in order to be seen as doing the work.</li>
        <li>It will not ask you to make the guide more important than your own discernment.</li>
      </ul>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light" spacing="compact">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="How this work is offered">
        <p>Same spine. Different rooms.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The Remembering may take the form of a group journey, private mentorship, or an
          immersive experience. Specific dates and structures are shared when an offering is
          open. Until then, a fit conversation is how we discern whether group, private, or
          another doorway is the right next step.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section surface="light">
    <Container width="narrow">
      <SectionIntro heading="Questions">
        <p>What people usually want to know before they step closer.</p>
      </SectionIntro>
      <FaqList>
        <FaqItem question="Do I need to read the book first?">
          <p>
            No. The book can deepen the language and context. Participation does not depend on
            completing assigned reading.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Do I need to identify as spiritual?">
          <p>
            No. Spiritual language may appear, but belief is not required. Curiosity,
            discernment, and a willingness to examine your own experience are enough.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Will I have to talk about trauma?">
          <p>
            No. There is no requirement to disclose traumatic experience or prove vulnerability.
            You choose what you share. Material that requires trauma treatment belongs with an
            appropriately qualified professional.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="Will I have to talk about sex?">
          <p>
            No. Embodiment, intimacy, sensuality, and body sovereignty may be discussed
            conceptually. Personal sexual disclosure is never required.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="What if I do not believe in archetypes?">
          <p>
            That is fine. Archetypes can be treated as metaphors or lenses rather than literal
            truths. Use what creates useful reflection and leave what does not.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="What if I am already in therapy?">
          <p>
            Therapy and this work may coexist when their roles stay clear. Therapy addresses
            what belongs in clinical care. She Who Remembers focuses on reflection, embodiment,
            self-trust, integration, and choice. It is not a substitute for treatment.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
        <FaqItem question="How do I choose group or private work?">
          <p>
            Group work can be useful when shared reflection and community matter. Private
            guidance offers more individualized attention around a specific threshold. A fit
            conversation can help determine which container makes more sense.
          </p>
        </FaqItem>
      </FaqList>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <SiteCta
    heading="If this is the season of return"
    primary={{ label: 'Book a Fit Conversation', href: withBase('/book-a-conversation') }}
    secondary={{ label: 'Begin Here', href: withBase('/begin-here') }}
  >
    <p>
      You do not need a polished reason. Bring the mismatch you can already feel. We will
      discern together whether The Remembering is the right room.
    </p>
  </SiteCta>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .core-question {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    border: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-quote);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: var(--leading-heading);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .fit,
  .not {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .fit li,
  .not li {
    position: relative;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
  }

  .fit li:last-child,
  .not li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .fit li::before,
  .not li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.7em;
    width: 0.4rem;
    height: 0.4rem;
    border: var(--border-width) solid var(--border-accent);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .topics {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .movements {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-lg);
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .movements li {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .movements li:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .movements span {
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-heading);
  }

  .work-link {
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .topics {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: var(--space-xl);
    }
  }
</style>
